.TH OPENNHRPCTL 8 "18 Aug 2026" "" "OpenNHRP Documentation"

.SH NAME
opennhrpctl \- opennhrp administrative control tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opennhrpctl
.BI "[\-a " admin\-socket "]" " command " "[" "arguments" "]..."

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opennhrpctl
is an utility to control
.BR opennhrp (8)
daemon operation. A UNIX socket is used for communication between
.B opennhrpctl
and
.BR opennhrp (8).
Administration priviledges for a non-root user can be granted by modifying
the permissions and ownership of the socket.

The following commands are available:

.BI "ha cluster init --interface " interface-name " --member-id " member-id " --advertise-address " address " ..."
.RS
Initialize a managed cluster. The shared protocol address and prefix are
derived from the interface's unique active IPv4 address. The command creates a
cluster ID, keyring, identity, member manifest, and authenticated state without
overwriting an existing managed cluster. The initial member has priority 100
and becomes the term 1 leader.
.RE

.BI "ha invite create --member-id " member-id " [--priority " priority "] [--expires " duration "] [--format plain]"
.br
.B "ha invite list"
.br
.BI "ha invite revoke --id-prefix " prefix
.br
.BI "ha invite delete --id-prefix " prefix
.RS
Create, inspect, revoke, or permanently delete a signed one-time enrollment
Invite. Delete accepts unused, expired, claimed, and revoked Invites, but only
on the current Leader; deleting a claimed Invite does not remove its Hub
member. Creation does not take an interface argument. Invite output contains a
secret and must be handled as sensitive input; list output exposes only an ID
prefix and metadata.
.RE

.BI "ha join --interface " interface-name " [--advertise-address " address "] ..."
.RS
Join a managed cluster using an Invite read from standard input. Interactive
input is read without echo; non-interactive input consumes one line. The Invite
cannot be passed in argv. The local interface address and prefix must exactly
match the shared protocol address in the Invite.
Up to four addresses may be supplied in preference order. The Leader merges
them with the authenticated TCP source address observed during enrollment.
.RE

.B "ha members show"
.br
.BI "ha member set " member-id " --priority " priority
.br
.BI "ha member set " member-id " --advertise-address " address " ..."
.br
.BI "ha member enable " member-id
.br
.BI "ha member disable " member-id
.br
.BI "ha member remove " member-id
.RS
Inspect and modify the managed member manifest. A member must be disabled
before removal. The current leader cannot be disabled, and the fixed Primary
cannot be removed.
Enabling a disabled member returns it as a learner; it becomes active only
after catching up with the Leader.
When one or more advertised addresses are supplied, they atomically replace
the member's configured address list; an automatically observed address is
retained when it remains distinct and the combined list has room.
.RE

.BI "ha key export-spoke --output " absolute-file
.br
.B "ha key rotate prepare"
.br
.B "ha key rotate commit"
.RS
Export the cluster authentication keyring for a Spoke or perform a two-key
rotation. Secret key material is never included in status JSON.
Copy an exported keyring through a trusted channel to
.IR /etc/opennhrp/ha/interface.keys
on the Spoke and set owner-only mode 0600. The map configuration itself does
not contain a keyring path.
.RE

.BI "ha show interface " interface-name " [format json]"
.RS
Show shared gateway services, activation and internal Hub List revisions, list
source, active member, candidate origin, effective local NBMA and its source,
per-candidate warm registration, and adaptive probe state.
.RE

.BI "ha monitor interface " interface-name
.RS
Keep the management connection open and stream one JSON object whenever HA
state changes. This is the input used by
.BR opennhrp-ha (8).
.RE

.B "ha cluster show --format json"
.br
.B "ha witness show --format json"
.br
.B "ha replication show --format json"
.br
.B "ha key status --format json"
.br
.B "ha failback request [force]"
.br
.B "ha failback show --format json"
.RS
When directed to the Hub coordinator control socket, show term/Leader,
quorum, Witness, replication commit/match/digest, key, and failback state, or
request a safe failback. Managed Backup Leaders automatically transfer
leadership after the Primary is authenticated and healthy for 120 seconds and
registration state is synchronized. The JSON view reports health,
synchronization, pending transfer, probation, and backoff state. Force skips
time gates only; authentication, health, replication synchronization, quorum,
and the authenticated leadership transfer remain mandatory.
.RE

.BI "ha witness prepare epoch " 32-hex-epoch
.br
.BI "ha witness activate epoch " 32-hex-epoch
.br
.BI "ha witness lease epoch " 32-hex-epoch " term " term " holder " member-id " sequence " sequence " ttl-ms " milliseconds
.RS
Manager-facing commands for an exactly two-active-Hub cluster. Send each
command to every Hub coordinator socket. Prepare installs a nonzero epoch and
fences service during staging; activate enables Manager Witness quorum. Lease
selects the unique holder and must use a nondecreasing term, strictly
increasing sequence, and TTL from 1 through 3000 milliseconds. These commands
are not needed when three or more active Hubs use Hub majority.
.RE

.BI "[cache] show [" selector "]..."
.RS
Show contents of next hop cache (configured and resolved entries).
.RE

.BI "[cache] flush [" selector "]..."
.RS
Clear all non-permanent entries which match the selector specifiers.
.RE

.BI "[cache] purge [" selector "]..."
.RS
Purge entries from NHRP cache: cached entries are removed and permanent
entries are forced down, up and finally reregistered.
.RE

.BI "[cache] lowerdown [" selector "]..."
.RS
Purge entries from NHRP cache with indication that lower layer failed:
e.g. IPsec daemon detected dead-peer or received INITIIAL-CONTACT
notification.
.RE

.BI "[cache] renew [" selector "]..."
.RS
Immediately send a new registration request for matching static maps that
were configured with the \fBregister\fR option. Static maps without that
option are not affected.
.RE

.BI "route show [" selector "]..."
.RS
Show the contents of locally cached kernel routing information
(outbound routing base to do route lookups excluding active shortcut
routes).
.RE

.B "interface show"
.RS
Show the contents of interface configuration table, and the cached information
from kernel (like protocol and NBMA IP addresses in use currently).
.RE

.BI "redirect purge [" protocol-address "/" prefix-length "]"
.RS
Clear redirection cache from all entries matching the specified address.
.RE

.BI "update nbma " nbma-address " " protocol-address
.RS
This command can be used from
.BR opennhrp-script "(8)"
to inform
.BR opennhrp
daemon of the real
.IR protocol-address
of dynamically discovered NHS.
.RE

.B "reload"
.RS
Reload configuration file (/etc/opennhrp/opennhrp.conf) differentially without restarting opennhrp daemon. Dynamic peer registrations from Spoke clients remain untouched.
.RE

.BI "map add " interface " " protocol-address " " nbma-address|hostname " [local-nbma " local-nbma-address "] [register] [cisco] [no-unique]"
.RS
Add a new static map or update an existing static map dynamically at runtime in memory.
.RE

.BI "map del [" interface "] " protocol-address
.RS
Delete an existing static map dynamically at runtime from memory.
.RE

.B "map save"
.RS
Save current configuration and all static maps from memory to configuration file (/etc/opennhrp/opennhrp.conf).
.RE

The following selectors can be used to limit which cache entries will
be effected:

.BI nbma " nbma-address"
.RS
Matches entries where the remote has NBMA address
.IR nbma-address .
.RE

.BI protocol " protocol-address" "[/" "prefix-length" "]"
.RS
Matches entries where the remote has protocol address
.IR protocol-address " with at least prefix length " prefix-length .
.RE

.BI local-nbma " nbma-address"
.RS
Matches entries from local interface which owns the NBMA address
.IR nbma-address .
.RE

.BI local-protocol " protocol-address"
.RS
Matches entries only from local interface which owns the protocol address
.IR protocol-address .
.RE

.BI interface " interface-name"
.br
.BI iface " interface-name"
.br
.BI dev " interface-name"
.RS
Search entries only from local interface with name
.IR interface-name .
.RE

.RE

.SH FILES
.I /var/run/opennhrp.socket
.RS
.BR opennhrp "(8) control socket"
.RE

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR opennhrp (8)
.BR opennhrp-ha (8)

